            "description": ".. image:: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cupy/cupy/master/docs/image/cupy_logo_1000px.png\r\n   :width: 400\r\n\r\nCuPy : NumPy & SciPy for GPU\r\n============================\r\n\r\n`CuPy <https://cupy.dev/>`_ is a NumPy/SciPy-compatible array library for GPU-accelerated computing with Python.\r\n\r\nThis is a CuPy wheel (precompiled binary) package for CUDA 12.x.\r\nYou need to install `CUDA Toolkit 12.x <https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-toolkit-archive>`_ to use these packages.\r\n\r\nIf you have another version of CUDA, or want to build from source, refer to the `Installation Guide <https://docs.cupy.dev/en/latest/install.html>`_ for instructions.\r\n",
